  message: "Dogfooding re-confirmed (blinded severity 3/5): fingerprint=None on ~3911 Python methods (12.6% of py method+func nodes; zero non-test py methods). Root reproduced fresh on a NEW file (test_ruby.py): a triple-quoted fixture embedding `class Order < ApplicationRecord` at column 0 makes textwrap.dedent compute common-prefix=0, so the `def` stays indented → ast.parse raises IndentationError → returns None. Same _python_ast_fingerprint dedent/parse fix. [dogfood]"  # 34ab
- op: discuss  # 078f
